 ],
 "literal": "Rain wild-jasmine's water-dripping fat bud / dark palmyra's green sheath many together having enclosed / great rain dawn having expanded like / she is of fragrant coolness, good dark complexion / water-raft like beautiful joints bamboo-like shoulders / uniting and parting we do not have / if separating, living, even more than that, we do not have",
 "translation": "Like the fat, water-dripping buds of the wild jasmine in the rainy season, wrapped together in the green sheath of a dark palmyra tree and then blossomed at the dawn of a heavy downpour, she is of fragrant coolness. Her body has a beautiful dark complexion, and her bamboo-like shoulders with lovely joints are like a raft on the water. We have neither a formal union nor a parting; and if we were to separate, we would have no life at all.",
 "modern": "மழைக்காலத்து முல்லை மலரின் நீர்வடியும் கொழுவிய மொட்டுகளை, கரிய பனைமரத்தின் பசிய மடலில் பலவற்றையும் ஒன்றாகச் சேர்த்து மூடிவைத்து, பெருமழை பெய்த விடியற்காலத்தில் மலரச் செய்தது போன்ற நறுமணமும் குளிர்ச்சியும் உடையவள் அவள். நல்ல மாந்தளிர் போன்ற நிறமும், நீரில் மிதக்கும் புணையைப் போன்ற அழகிய மூட்டுகளையுடைய மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களும் கொண்ட அவளைக் கூடுதல் என்பதும் பிரிதல் என்பதும் நமக்கு இல்லை. அவளைப் பிரிந்தால் உயிர் வாழ்தல் என்பது அதைவிடவும் நமக்கு இல்லை.",
 "explanation": "The hero speaks to his heart when he contemplates leaving his beloved to earn wealth, realizing that separation is impossible. He describes her fragrant coolness by comparing her to wild jasmine buds that have been kept wrapped in a green palmyra sheath and then opened fresh at a rainy dawn. Her shoulders are as supportive and beautiful as a raft on water, and her complexion is of a beautiful dark hue. He declares that they have never truly experienced a separate union or parting because they are always one in spirit. Therefore, if they were to physically separate, survival itself would be completely out of the question.",
